It is a quiet Sunday morning in June.
I wake up quite late.
I get up slowly and make myself a coffee.
It is wonderfully peaceful in the flat.
On Sundays, ordinary shops are shut here.
I have no plans today and do not have to be anywhere.
I stand at the window and look outside.
This morning is bright and warm.
The morning is simply perfect.
I think about my early days in Berlin.
I arrived here exactly five months ago.
Back then in January, it was freezing cold and dark.
This city was still very unfamiliar to me.
The city feels completely different now.
My life has changed so much since then.
I drink my coffee and smile.
I am looking forward to this summer.
The summer in Berlin will definitely be nice.
